  "_about": "The GRIFFIN (2026-11-07): an eagle in front, a lion behind -- the lion's body, rig, gait, hindquarters and tufted tail (mammals/lion.json), and the golden eagle's head with a bigger hooked beak, its breast and neck feathered (the lion's chest, withers and forelegs painted in its plumage, crossfading into the fur over the waist), an eagle's forelegs -- feathered to the wrist, then the yellow scaled shank and four toes with black talons -- and its wings (birds/eagle.json: arm, hand and feather rows) scaled 2.6x onto the withers, a span of about 4.3 m. ROUND 2: the eagle's brow ridge over each eye, ear tufts, a ruff of hackles down the neck into the breast; the front's plumage in the birds' row scales, the lion's coat ticked (agouti) behind, crossfading over the waist; the head carried lower. Built at the lion's size and then 1.15x it (`scaleBy`). The wings are drawn SPREAD; on the ground they are folded along the flanks (skeleton.js PERCH; skysteeds.js SKYSTEEDS.griffin), and it flies as the pegasus does (skysteeds.js). Its coats: golden (a tawny lion, a golden-brown eagle), white-headed (a bald eagle's white head and dark brown plumage) and dark. SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- elower, eupper (2 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator.",
